+# Registered conversion callback at 0x008C6AD0
+
+## Scope and baseline
+
+The baseline is `3d3b0681294a0de92aae10ea1a753ae22068f091`.
+`ea_evidence.csv` assigns this callback to
+`Libraries/Source/Apt/AptActionInterpreter.cpp`. Its proper local home is
+`game/Libraries/Source/Apt/AptActionInterpreter.cpp`. That whole translation
+unit contains one existing matched body, `rva8CF1B0ProcessRecord` at
+`0x008CF1B0`, 520 bytes. The existing source prefix is unchanged.
+
+The new callback keeps the bank's address-qualified name
+`BooleanCoerce008C6AD0(void *, int)`. Neither this descriptive name nor the
+inline helper is presented as an original EA function name. The registration
+in `Rva0089BBF0InitGlobals.cpp` places the address in a built-in callback
+object, without proving a more specific source-level identity.
+
+Both the new callback and the existing same-file body are covered by official
+claim lease `fd901b9cef4049468a07d3aad4b4df9e`, claim commit
+`2eaf3e0ac530cd53f2ecf4cf4aa2a18346935f6b`, owned by
+`github:mcmickey93:bfme1:cpp-loop-2` and expiring at 2026-10-25 13:29:43 UTC.
+
+## Boundary and ABI
+
+The complete decode begins at `0x008C6AD0`. The last `ret` is at offset
+`+0xE8`; padding begins at `+0xE9`, establishing the 233-byte extent.
+The zero-argument-count path returns at `+0x0D`; the remaining return paths
+end at `+0xAB`, `+0xC6`, `+0xDC` and `+0xE8`. All conditional destinations
+remain inside the body. The function reads the second stack argument as its
+count, leaves arguments on the caller's stack, and returns a pointer in EAX.
+Its first stack argument is unused in these bytes.
+
+The value flags occupy offset +4, with the low six type bits and validity
+bit 15. Boolean payload reads use offset +8. The existing matched numeric
+converter and Boolean factory independently witness these fields. The
+canonical numeric predicate also provides a verified C++ validity-bitfield
+view; it is a source-context lead, not proof that this callback matches.
+
+The three distinct direct callees are already matched:
+
+| RVA | Existing declaration | Call evidence here |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `0x008983D0` | `float AptValue::toNumber()` | ECX receiver, no stack argument, result consumed on x87 stack |
+| `0x008996B0` | `AptBoolean *AptBoolean::Create(bool)` | One stack argument, caller removes four bytes, pointer result in EAX |
+| `0x008C4A30` | `bool __cdecl Rva008C4A30Check(Rva8CD130Value *)` | One pointer pushed at +0x7D, caller removes four bytes, tests AL |
+
+The predicate's 873-byte recovery and its independent caller and unwind
+checks are documented in `008c4a30-numeric-predicate.md`. The bank's
+`void d_008c4a30()` cast is replaced by that proven typed declaration.
+No new callee binding is needed.
+
+## Data bindings
+
+The bank's `g_bfmeCount1233` pin points at the old `0x00F38748` address.
+The candidate instead reuses `Rva008AE770TheStack`, pinned at VA
+`0x01338748`, with the same twelve-byte prefix as the adjacent matched
+`0x008C6800` callback: count at +0, an unused word at +4, and the value-array
+pointer at +8. The fallback pointer reuses `g_bfmeFallbackDB` at
+`0x013379BC`, whose four-byte storage already has a matched data row.
+
+The numeric comparison reuses the matched data owner `g_rva01075350`.
+Its four bytes at VA `0x01075350` are `00 00 00 00`, and the retail callback
+loads it from memory before `fucompp`. An extern float declaration preserves
+that access; replacing it with a folded literal could change the instruction
+shape. The preferred bank's unbound `BfmeZeroRange` name is not carried over.
+
+## Bounded experiment
+
+The preferred bank remains unchanged. Its three existing verdicts describe
+an important unresolved control-flow constraint: retail keeps four Boolean
+factory call blocks, including two separate false blocks at +0xA0 and
++0xD1, while sharing the numeric-conversion tail. The previously tried nine
+if/switch/ternary/Boolean-output forms produced a 217-byte merged body or
+260--272-byte alternatives. Those trials are not repeated here.
+
+Seven complete-file candidates isolate the new context hypotheses:
+
+1. `00-canonical-control.cpp` preserves the bank's raw-shift predicates and
+   free inline coercion helper, while fixing its typed callee and data bindings.
+2. `01-native-validity.cpp` adds the validity-bitfield representation already
+   used by the matched predicate, keeping the same free inline helper.
+3. `02-native-member-context.cpp` also makes coercion an inline value member,
+   so the value and its typed predicates share a native member context.
+4. `03-split-false-barriers.cpp` starts from corrected control 00 and tags
+   the common false-return paths with `_WriteBarrier()`, while tagging only
+   the coercion default-false path with `_ReadWriteBarrier()`. It is the
+   first native experiment, with the measured result recorded below;
+   00--02 have not been compiled here.
+5. `04-after-call-barriers.cpp` moves those same barrier tags after the
+   factory calls, keeping each zero-code marker inside its return suffix.
+   It also loads the stack array into a local before indexing by the count,
+   following the already matched `Rva008C6800.cpp` callback's statement order.
+   Its measured result is recorded below.
+6. `05-flat-cfg-barriers.cpp` keeps 04's corrected stack-array local and
+   replaces the inline coercion split with explicit labels in the retail
+   block order: numeric, common false, payload coercion, default false,
+   common true. The proven distinct false-tail barrier tags remain. Earlier
+   goto trials lacked effective tail separation; this is the combined
+   control-flow test after that prerequisite changed, not a repeat of them.
+   Its measured result is recorded below.
+7. `06-helper-entry-barrier.cpp` returns to 04's inline helper and passes
+   the already cached low-six-bit type as an explicit parameter. A single
+   `_ReadWriteBarrier()` at the helper's entry tests whether an optimization
+   boundary there preserves the caller's numeric/false fall-through before
+   the coercion block. Passing the type avoids a flags reload across that
+   barrier. Both existing after-call false-tail tags and the array-local
+   load order remain unchanged. This is the next finite native experiment;
+   the source boundary is a hypothesis, not a guarantee of block placement.
+
+The fourth experiment follows the specific tail-cross-jump technique in
+`docs/shape_levers.md`, independently witnessed by the already matched
+`stlport_narrow_string_find_char_alias.cpp` at `0x00653990` (69 bytes) and
+`LinePassableStruct_linePassableCallback.cpp` at `0x003E5950` (203 bytes).
+Those examples retain two identical return tails with distinct barrier
+intrinsics, and direct a third site to the desired common tail by using the
+same intrinsic there. Neither intrinsic emits code in those witnesses.
+
+Here the common false block must be shared by fallback, numeric-predicate
+and equal-number exits; the coercion default false block must stay separate.
+Experiment 03 placed the barriers immediately before the Boolean factory
+calls. It retained four factory blocks, but moved the shared numeric block
+and inverted its final branch, as measured below. Experiment 04 puts the
+barrier after the factory call to test whether the retained return suffixes
+keep that block at its original location. This is a separate code-layout
+hypothesis, not a byte-exact claim from applying a source pattern. No earlier target attempt recorded this
+barrier family. The true and payload-return paths are unchanged.
+
+They are retained under ignored `build/008c6ad0-canonical/`. None changes
+the existing 520-byte source prefix, adds assembly, changes a shared header,
+or adds a pin. A source spelling is only an experiment until the native
+compiler and the ordinary relocation-aware gate verify it.
